      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Heterotopic pregnancy is a rare event that usually presents in the first 6-8 weeks of pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE",
          "content": "A 35-year-old primigravida was referred to the hospital at 18+ weeks' gestational age for evaluation of chronic abdominal pain. Ultrasound revealed a heterotopic pregnancy. The patient underwent surgery for removal of the ectopic pregnancy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Heterotopic pregnancy can present at any time during pregnancy and should be considered in any pregnant woman with abdominal pain."
        }
      ]},
